## SEVERITY / VERDICT (the grading rule is decided HERE; apply it, do not re-argue it)
*Blocker:* a path beyond the five; a commit count other than 2; a head or base blob other than those named; a removed `.cs` line; a changed byte of `FollowUpModels.cs`, `invisible-characters.json`, `openapi.yaml`, `Problems.cs`, any `web/**`, `infra/**`, `.github/**`, csproj or any existing test; a new user-facing string other than the 8 ruled sentences, or a sentence not byte-equal to its field's ruled sentence; **any scalar of the 212 ACCEPTED on any of the 10 field-routes** (including a cross-wired check, or a check not reached on PUT); **a check that reads the trimmed value or is not reached when the value is blank after a trim (C3)**; **any difference between base and head outside the refused set (over-refusal, a changed stored value, status or body for a kept plant) (C4)**; a refusal that is not a 400 `application/problem+json` with the field's code and wire name; a refusal after which anything is stored or an ETag moved; a new row red, skipped or missing on SQLite or on SQL Server (C6); a failed test beyond the two named `PkcsInPackageTests` rows in any run of the head; a red or cancelled non-environmental check-run; a CodeQL alert open on the head (either threshold), a missing analysis at the verdict, or an alert dismissed other than by the org; a textual conflict (C9); the head moved; a secret; a non-ASCII byte, a person's name, a decision-card id or a `B###` token in an added line or any commit message; a skip, sleep, retry, environment or provider gate.
*Major, class SAME (the class is "control-character refusal by the shared predicate added to Api free-text write fields"):* **(M1) a call site that does not call the shared `FollowUpShape.HasControl`, or a mutant of C10 (Y1-Y10, Y12-Y16) that leaves BOTH your matrix and the builder's class green, not shown equivalent by a run;** **(M2) refusal changes the stored state or an ETag** (also a Blocker when measured; this line grades a path where only a partial write is shown); **(M3) a write path to one of the eight columns that bypasses the checks (C8c)** (an unchecked second route is a Major SAME with the route named); **(M4) a comment, README sentence or doc line the repository contradicts**; *Major FOR TUESDAY (not a branch failure, the B478-1 shape):* a refused scalar reachable through the product's own flows (generation, templates, import, the web's own PUT body) so that a user can no longer save through the web (C8b), with the evidence; the builder's choice of NO allowance is the product owner's coordinator's stamped ruling, so this is reported for Tuesday's call, not graded against the branch.
*Major, class DIFFERENT:* a builder claim contradicted by measurement with a verdict consequence (35 rows, 27 red at the base, 2028/0/13 against 1993/0/13, 16 of 16 mutants red, names lost 0 added 35, 44 contract tests).
*Minor / Note (never a Major):* the Y11b survivor of the builder's rows (the rows pin 3 of 212 scalars; the property is pinned by the shared function's own test and by your matrix); the 400 here versus the 422 of the answer note (by design); a list holding the new code AND a blank/length code for a value that is only a refused white-space scalar (by design, first error read); the evidence route having no web caller; the web mock not knowing the eight fields; a noun that differs from a web label; the held-value case when reachable only by a direct write; the lone-surrogate behaviour on these fields (record it, the table does not list it); the unsigned commits; the first commit red at itself; the PR body's model trailer; GitHub's runner timing; the `databases` figure differing from 284; minor tool-version differences from the runner.
*Where the line between Note and Major is unclear:* a thing that lets a refused character in, or turns a legitimate value away, is at least Blocker; a thing that makes a pin unable to fail is at least Major SAME; a thing that changes only what a message or a comment says and stays true is a Note. Say which rule you applied for every finding.
**VERDICT RULES.** GO needs Checks 1 to 10 clean and measured, both CodeQL thresholds met on a COMPLETE scan (4 of 4 analyses at `bcb359f`, 0 open alerts), every check-run `completed` `success` EXCEPT the named environmental reds of C6 which you SHOWED fail only on the two `PkcsInPackageTests` rows, the 35 new names read `Passed` in the `api-assessment` shard's results, 0 findings above Note; the verdict then carries `(environmental CI red: the Pkcs pin lane, 2 rows, <check names>; landing waits for that lane)`. **While any check-run of the head is pending the verdict is at most GO WITH FINDINGS and its text carries `(conditional: CI pending: <names>)`, never a bare GO; while `api-assessment` is pending add `SQL Server rows not yet read`.** GO WITH FINDINGS = Minor/Note only (and Major FOR TUESDAY items, which ride in FOR TUESDAY without capping the verdict unless Tuesday asks). NO GO on any Blocker or Major SAME/DIFFERENT; this is round 1 of 2, so a NO GO here does NOT reach the round cap: STATUS gives each Major's mutant or plant (diff against the head file), the red set by name (or "none: green"), your run's output and a fix-shape in prose, and whether ONE new commit on the same branch fixes it. NOT GATED = the head moved, the PR is not open, or a moved guarded region. A security-shaped finding (a refused class accepted on a write path) is a STOP for tier 1: finish STATUS and end `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY`.
**VERDICT LINES (one place, binding).** **First line of STATUS (placeholder at Step 0: `GATE VERDICT B729: PENDING`; verdict form, one line):** `GATE VERDICT B729: #223 <GO|GO WITH FINDINGS|NO GO|NOT GATED> @ bcb359f (round 1 of 2 on class "control-character refusal by the shared predicate added to Api free-text write fields" - NO GO 0 of 2 before this gate - delta <2 commits, 5 paths, numstat y/n; blobs y/n; removed .cs lines 0 y/n; added lines placed y/n; FollowUpModels/table/contract/Problems/web/infra bytes 0 y/n; hygiene y/n> - reach <212 scalars x 3 positions x 10 field-routes: accepted <n> (expected 0), disagree with oracle <n>; base accepts all refused y/n; controls answer-note and customer name same partition y/n; collateral fields accept y/n> - as-sent <white-space edge plants refused <n of n>; only-content plants new code first y/n> - over-refusal <kept plants n; base vs head differences outside the refused set <n>> - words <8 of 8 byte-equal y/n; extra literals 0 y/n; README true y/n> - SQL Server <api-assessment completed success y/n; 35 new names Passed y/n; trx read y/n; outcomes n (main 1165); databases n floor 100> - environment <failed tests in api and api-other beyond the two Pkcs rows: n; same two rows red in another PR's run y/n; green at main y/n> - CI <n completed success of n; pending <names|none>; environmental red <names|none>; CodeQL umbrella <conclusion>; Api.Tests n> - CodeQL <analyses n of 4 at the head; open alerts n; dismissed n> - held value <PUT body sends title back y/n; reachable through product flows y/n (Major FOR TUESDAY y/n)> - census <write sites n, all checked y/n> - mutants <Y1-Y17 n built, red as predicted n, survivors <names|none>; Y11b survives the builder's rows y/n; c0 y/n; cw-weak y/n; c-fail y/n; seeded n of 3> - merge <mergeable_state; merge-tree vs main <sha7> rc n; tree equals GitHub's y/n; shared paths with #221, #222, the Pkcs lane 0 y/n; main still b069274 y/n> - gitleaks rc <n>)`. Then the sections: Step 0 (sh