**STATUS-NOW (binding).** **Write the STATUS file at Step 0 and keep it updated; a STATUS that does not exist while your logs move is a failure of this brief.** At Step 0, before any heavy work, write `/Volumes/Laptop-DEV/!CODING/Datasec/HPSM-POC/1_Project_Definition/Briefs/2026-10-26_B729_STATUS.md` holding: the placeholder FIRST line `GATE VERDICT B729: PENDING`; Step 0 (sha256 of the brief and its copy, the slot count with its control, your Step-0 date with the target verdict and HARD STOP written absolute, the model line); the REFUSE counts; PINS (the head, main, `compare` ahead/behind, the open-PR list, `mergeable_state`, check-run counts and CodeQL analysis count at your start); and one line per check (1-10) saying done / running / not started, with the evidence path of what is done. While working the LAST line is `WORKING: <part> <time>`; write no `VERDICT:` or `STOPPED:` line at a line start until you mean it (a watcher fires on those). Update after every check and every mutant batch. Evidence goes in `Briefs/2026-10-26_B729_evidence/` (summaries, hashes, TSVs, test-output excerpts, CI extracts; no secrets, no scripts, no person's name). At about 80% of your context or at the hard stop write `## PROGRESS and RESUME` (per check done/partial/not started, next exact commands, every scratch mutant with its restore proof), stop every process of yours, release the lock, and end the FILE with `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY continue in a fresh seat from RESUME?`.
